<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE policyconfig PUBLIC
 "-//freedesktop//DTD PolicyKit Policy Configuration 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/PolicyKit/1/policyconfig.dtd">

<!--
  APEX Shell — the password behind "Always unrestricted agents"

  ROADMAP.md §42.1 asks that turning the APEX sandbox OFF for new sessions take
  a real local password at a prompt the agent cannot reach, and that turning it
  back ON again be immediate and ask for nothing. This action is that password.

  Config → Agents raises it by running pkcheck against this action id, for the
  shell's own process, with user interaction allowed, and writes
  ~/.config/apex/agent.json only when that exits 0. The argv is in
  src/services/AgentPolicyService.qml rather than quoted here: an XML comment
  may not contain a double hyphen, and every flag it uses starts with one.

  ── auth_self, not auth_admin ───────────────────────────────────────────────

  The setting does not grant root and must not be authenticated as though it
  did. It changes which sandbox the user's own agent sessions start in, and the
  invariants in apex-agent-core hold either way: a session keeps
  PR_SET_NO_NEW_PRIVS whichever sandbox it has, and secrets stay behind the
  broker. auth_admin would ask the wrong question and, on a single-user
  machine, teach the user to type the root password at a dialog that is not
  about root.

  What the prompt is actually for is presence: a human at this keyboard, now.
  auth_self asks exactly that.

  ── and not auth_self_keep ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

  _keep caches the authorization for the rest of the session, which is a window
  in which the answer is yes without anybody being asked. The whole value of
  the prompt is that it happens every time the default moves toward
  unrestricted, so there is no cached yes to inherit.

  ── allow_inactive and allow_any are no ─────────────────────────────────────

  A switched-away session and a remote one are both "nobody is at this
  keyboard", and §7 reserves elevation for a local origin. There is no
  password that makes them local, so they are refused outright rather than
  challenged.

  Install (regular systemd host):
    sudo install -Dm644 dots-extra/polkit/org.apexos.shell.agent.policy \
         /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.apexos.shell.agent.policy

  Image builds (e.g. APEX-OS): ship it read-only at the same path.

  polkitd re-reads actions on change. Until it is installed, pkcheck exits 127
  with "is not registered" and the toggle says so instead of failing silently.
-->

<policyconfig>

  <vendor>APEX Shell</vendor>
  <vendor_url>https://github.com/AndreNijman/apex-shell</vendor_url>

  <action id="org.apexos.shell.agent.set-always-unrestricted">
    <description>Start new agents with no APEX sandbox</description>
    <message>Authentication is required to let new agent sessions read and write your whole home directory.</message>
    <defaults>
      <allow_any>no</allow_any>
      <allow_inactive>no</allow_inactive>
      <allow_active>auth_self</allow_active>
    </defaults>
  </action>

</policyconfig>
